=== talk-rep

--- start
REP-X: "Everyone thinks introducing a bill is the hard part." They gesture at a shelf of binders, none of them yours. "Forty-one measures have my name on them this session. Three of them I'd take a bad meeting for. Tell me again why yours is one of the three."
PROCEDURE: Forty-one introductions, and a member's real currency is which ones they spend a chair's patience on. You are asking for that, not for a signature.
BASE BUILDING: They want to know the people behind it are real. Give them a district and a name, not a coalition letterhead.

* Give them the district numbers. Their district.
  {+4 house}
  They read it twice. "Eleven hundred households in my precincts alone?" It goes in the top folder, which is a smaller folder than it sounds.

* "Because you'll be the one who passed it."
  {+2 house, +1 influence}
  "Flattery." A pause. "Effective flattery, but flattery."
